From: 0racl-lab <360770237+0racl-lab@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 17:41:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Add read_content service (interface 7)

Fetches a file from the operator's IPFS gateways, Arweave gateways or content
mirrors, keeps only bytes whose SHA-256 matches the query, and returns the
size, a byte range or one JSON field (strict I-JSON, RFC 8785 canonical
output). Missing (404, wrong bytes, oversize) is NOT_FOUND; a failing source
makes the service abstain. Stdlib-only Python with mock gateways and a
selftest (45 checks). Node config, docker-compose and example_env register
slot 7. Requires the matching qubic/core interface (ContentRead.h).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QHXGjDwxBARUytE2smA8oq
